### Demo requests (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client)
@gateway = http://localhost:5000
# For docker-compose use: @gateway = http://localhost:8080

### 1) Issue a development token for a customer
# @name customerToken
POST {{gateway}}/auth/dev-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "customer-42",
  "roles": ["Customer"],
  "scopes": ["accounts:read", "payments:write"]
}

### 2) List accounts (role + scope + per-user quota)
GET {{gateway}}/api/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken.response.body.accessToken}}
X-Correlation-ID: demo-accounts-001

### 3) Create a payment (repeat > 10 times within 60s to observe HTTP 429)
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccountId": "ACC-00001-TRY",
  "toIban": "TR00 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 01",
  "amount": 1250.50,
  "currency": "TRY"
}

### 4) Public endpoint (anonymous, IP-based quota)
GET {{gateway}}/api/public/fx-rates

### 5) Anonymous call to a protected route -> 401 + security event
GET {{gateway}}/api/accounts

### 6) Customer calling the audit endpoint -> 403 + security event
GET {{gateway}}/gateway/security-events
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7) Issue an auditor token
# @name auditorToken
POST {{gateway}}/auth/dev-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "auditor-01",
  "roles": ["Auditor"],
  "scopes": ["audit:read"]
}

### 8) Read the security audit trail
GET {{gateway}}/gateway/security-events?take=20&type=RateLimitExceeded
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9) Health probes (excluded from rate limiting)
GET {{gateway}}/health/ready
